# Trash and versions are server apps that an administrator can turn off (specs/006-trash-and-versions, Story 5): the screens say so in plain words and offer no
# tool that cannot work. Run last, with the same server: it turns the trash app off before this run starts.
# server trash-disable
# server versions-disable
size 1404 1872
waitfor homeState Connected to Example Cloud
tap homeTrash
waitfor trashExplain
shot @OUT@/230-trash-off.png
expect trashExplain This server has no trash
expect trashExplain cannot be listed or restored
expect trashExplain permanent
expect trashExplain administrator
expect_absent trashRow
expect_absent trashCheck
tap trashBack
waitfor homeState Connected to Example Cloud
# the versions app is off too: the versions screen of a file explains it and offers no restore (the app opens Files in the folder where the walk before left it)
tap homeFiles
waitfor folderPath 0-walk
waitfor folderRow
tap folderRow 0
waitfor detailsVersions
tap detailsVersions
waitfor versionsExplain
shot @OUT@/231-versions-off.png
expect versionsExplain does not keep older versions
expect versionsExplain cannot be listed or restored
expect versionsExplain administrator
expect_absent versionsRow
expect_absent versionsRestore
quit
